          "message": {
            "text": "The corpus is a finite deconfounded 348-cell union per run, not a diagonal fit matrix. Every technology covers sizes, weights, all sixteen quarter-pixel phases, every transform and DPR1/2; hinted glyf also crosses phase with rotate/affine. A canonical cell hash binds text, source bytes, axes, concrete matrix, paint plan and metric version so an envelope cannot migrate between superficially similar dimensions.",
